Cell[TextData[{
  "Suppose we like to represent a complex function Sin[",
  StyleBox["z",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "] graphically, where ",
  StyleBox["z",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " is a complex number.  How can we make a plot of a complex function?"
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "One way to do this is to consider the function as a mapping from a \
two-dimensional point ",
  StyleBox["z",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "=(",
  StyleBox["x,y",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ") to a new point ",
  StyleBox["f",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "(",
  StyleBox["z",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ") = (Re ",
  StyleBox["f",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ", Im ",
  StyleBox["f",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "). Such maps are called conformal maps in mathematics.  In fact, we \
consider the effect of how lines are mapped.  Specifically, we'll write a \
function which plot the image of the regular grid"
}], "Text"],

Cell[GraphicsData["PostScript", "\<\
