Cell["\<\
Question: which line is associated which line in the original regular grids?  \
The grids get distorted, but which feature(s) of the original grid is (are) \
still preserved?\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "I'll show you the code first, then explain slowly some of the features in \
the program that you have not seen.  I also demonstrate in class how such a \
program can be built-up and refined step-by-step.  The code is adapted from \
the standard ",
  StyleBox["Mathematica",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " package \"Graphics`ComplexMap`\". "
}], "Text"],

Cell["Complex map package", "Subtitle"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["BeginPackage[\"Graphics`ComplexMap`\"]\n\nUnprotect[ \
CartesianMap, Lines ]\n\nCartesianMap::usage = \"CartesianMap[f, {x0, x1, \
(dx)}, {y0, y1, (dy)}] plots the image of the cartesian coordinate lines \
under the function f. The default values of dx and dy are chosen so that the \
number of lines is equal to the value of the option Lines.\"\nLines::usage = \
\"Lines -> {lx, ly} is an option of CartesianMap that gives the number of \
lines to draw.\"\n\nBegin[\"`Private`\"]\n\n\
Needs[\"Utilities`FilterOptions`\"]\n\n$Lines = 15; (* global default *)\n\
Options[CartesianMap] = { Lines :> $Lines }\n\nCartesianMap[ func_, {x0_, \
x1_, dx_:Automatic}, {y0_, y1_, dy_:Automatic}, opts___?OptionQ ] :=\n    \
Module[ {x, y}, \n    \tPicture[ CartesianMap, func[x + I y], {x, x0, x1, \
dx}, {y, y0, y1, dy}, opts ]\n    ] /; NumericQ[x0] && NumericQ[x1] && \
NumericQ[y0] && NumericQ[y1] && \n     (NumericQ[dx] || dx === Automatic) && \
(NumericQ[dy] || dy === Automatic)\n\nPicture[ cmd_, e_, {s_, s0_, s1_, ds_}, \
{t_, t0_, t1_, dt_}, opts___ ] :=\n    Module[ {hg, vg, lines, nds = ds, ndt \
= dt},\n        lines = Lines /. {opts} /. Options[cmd];\n        If[ \
Head[lines] =!= List, lines = {lines, lines} ];\n        If[ ds === \
Automatic, nds = N[(s1-s0)/(lines[[1]]-1)] ];\n        If[ dt === Automatic, \
ndt = N[(t1-t0)/(lines[[2]]-1)] ];\n        hg = Curves[ e, {s, s0, s1, nds}, \
{t, t0, t1}, opts ];\n        vg = Curves[ e, {t, t0, t1, ndt}, {s, s0, s1}, \
opts ];\n        Show[ Graphics[ Join[hg, vg] ], FilterOptions[Graphics, \
opts],\n              AspectRatio -> Automatic, Axes -> True ] ]\n\nCurves[ \
xy_, spread_, bounds_, opts___ ] :=\n    With[{curves = Table[{Re[xy], \
Im[xy]}, spread]},\n        ParametricPlot[ curves, bounds, DisplayFunction \
-> Identity, Evaluate[FilterOptions[ParametricPlot, opts]] ][[1]] ]\n\nEnd[ ]\
\nProtect[ CartesianMap, Lines ]\nEndPackage[ ]",
  FontSize->12]], "Input",
  PageWidth->WindowWidth,
  ShowSpecialCharacters->False,
  FontSize->18],

Cell["Here is an example of how to use the code:", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(CartesianMap[Exp, \ {0, \ 1}, \ {0, \ 1}, \ 
      Lines\  \[Rule] \ 5]\)], "Input"],

