Cell["\<\
Now we are able to draw grids.  The next thing is to do the mapping. Rather \
than modify the above code, we do the mapping by a separate function, using \
the data generated by drawlines[ ].   The problem now is to relate each pair \
of point (x,y) by its image (Re f(x,y), Im f(x,y)).  The Map[ ] can be used.  \
Some test\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(f\ \  /@ {\ {x1, \ y1}, \ {x2, \ y2}}\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \({f[{x1, y1}], f[{x2, y2}]}\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(?Apply\)\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \("Apply[f, expr] or f @@ expr replaces the head of expr by f. Apply[f, \
expr, levelspec] replaces heads in parts of expr specified by levelspec."\)], \
"Print"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Apply[f, {{x1, y1}, \ {x2, \ y2}}, 2]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \({f[x1, y1], f[x2, y2]}\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
This also does not work, we need to convert {x,y} into x + I y.  Also, note \
that the return value from drawlines is { Line[{ {x1,y2}, ..}], ...}\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Map[\ #[\([1]\)]\  + \ I\ #[\([2]\)]\  &, \ {\ 
        Line[{{x1, y1}, \ {x2, \ y2}}]}, \ {3}]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \({Line[{x1 + \[ImaginaryI]\ y1, x2 + \[ImaginaryI]\ y2}]}\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(?Map\)\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \("Map[f, expr] or f /@ expr applies f to each element on the first level \
in expr. Map[f, expr, levelspec] applies f to parts of expr specified by \
levelspec."\)], "Print"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Map[{\ Re[f[#]], \ Im[f[#]]} &, \ %41]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \({{Re[f[x1 + \[ImaginaryI]\ y1]], 
        Im[f[x1 + \[ImaginaryI]\ y1]]}, {Re[f[x2 + \[ImaginaryI]\ y2]], 
        Im[f[x2 + \[ImaginaryI]\ y2]]}}\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["We put the above together as a module, ", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(cmap[f_, \ {x0_, \ x1_, \ dx_}, \ {y0_, \ y1_, \ dy_}]\  := \ 
      Module[{}, \ \[IndentingNewLine]ls\  = \ 
          drawlines[{x0, x1, \ dx}, \ {y0, \ y1, \ 
              dy}]; \[IndentingNewLine]z\  = \ 
          Map[\ \((#[\([1]\)]\  + \ I\ #[\([2]\)])\) &, \ 
            ls, \ {3}]; \[IndentingNewLine]\ 
        newlines\  = 
          Map[\ {Re[f[#]], \ Im[f[#]]} &, \ 
            z, \ {3}]\ \[IndentingNewLine]]\)], "Input"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(cmap[Identity, \ {0, \ 1, \ 0.5}, \ {0, 1, \ 0.5}]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \({Line[{{0, 0}, {0.5`, 0}, {1.`, 0}}], 
      Line[{{0, 0.5`}, {0.5`, 0.5`}, {1.`, 0.5`}}], 
      Line[{{0, 1.`}, {0.5`, 1.`}, {1.`, 1.`}}], 
      Line[{{0, 0}, {0, 0.5`}, {0, 1.`}}], 
      Line[{{0.5`, 0}, {0.5`, 0.5`}, {0.5`, 1.`}}], 
      Line[{{1.`, 0}, {1.`, 0.5`}, {1.`, 1.`}}]}\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Show[Graphics[cmap[Sin, {0, 1, 0.2}, \ {0, \ 1, \ 0.2}]], \ 
      AspectRatio \[Rule] \ Automatic]\)], "Input"],

