Cell["\<\
Now we can draw the images of set of horizontal lines and vertical lines \
separately.  But how can we draw them in the same plot?  One simple way is to \
say:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(hg\  = \ 
      Curves[Sin[x\  + \ I\ y], \ {y, \ 0.0, \ 1.0, \ 0.2}, \ {x, \ 0.0, \ 
          1.0}]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(hv\  = \ 
      Curves[Sin[x\  + \ I\ y], \ {x, \ 0.0, \ 1.0, \ 0.2}, \ {y, \ 0.0, \ 
          1.0}]\)], "Input"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(\(Show[hg, hv, \ 
      AspectRatio \[Rule] \ Automatic]\)\(\[IndentingNewLine]\)
    \)\)], "Input"],

