}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
However, you get three plots, one for horizontal lines, one for vertical \
lines, and the final combined lines.   We need to suppress the display of the \
first two plots.   Before doing this, let us see what is the FullForm of the \
graphics data structure hg or vg.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(FullForm[hg]\)], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
We see hg is   Graphics[{ {{Line[{{x,y}, ...}]}}, {{Line[{{..}}]}} }, \
{opt->r}].
To turn off the display of the graphics, but retaining the data structure, we \
use an option in plot function DisplayFunction -> Identity:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Curves[expr_, \ spread_, \ bounds_]\  := \ 
      With[{cvs\  = \ 
            Table[\ {Re[expr], \ Im[expr]}, \ 
              spread]}, \[IndentingNewLine]ParametricPlot[cvs, \ bounds, \ 
          DisplayFunction\  \[Rule] \ 
            Identity]\[IndentingNewLine]]\)], "Input"],

Cell["Now, we don't see the plot, but generate data only.", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(hg\  = \ 
      Curves[Sin[x\  + \ I\ y], \ {y, \ 0.0, \ 1.0, \ 0.2}, \ {x, \ 0.0, \ 
          1.0}]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    TagBox[\(\[SkeletonIndicator]  Graphics  \[SkeletonIndicator]\),
      False,
      Editable->False]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Show[hg]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    TagBox[\(\[SkeletonIndicator]  Graphics  \[SkeletonIndicator]\),
      False,
      Editable->False]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Show[Graphics[hg[\([1]\)]]]\)], "Input"],

